Invented by Johannes Gutenberg around 1440 in Mainz, Germany, the movable type printing press revolutionized the spread of information and marked the end of the medieval era. By mechanizing the process of printing, Gutenberg made books significantly cheaper and more accessible, breaking the monopoly of scribes and the church on knowledge. This technological breakthrough fueled the Renaissance, the Reformation, and the Scientific Revolution, as ideas could now travel rapidly across Europe, fundamentally
